      "writtenOn": "2015-03-14T14:44:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was not aware that port 35357 was supposed to receive only v2 requests. Is this new on Juno or Kilo versions?\nIn my icehouse installation, port 35357 can receive calls using the v3 API. I have tested calling:\nhttp://icehouse.sec.cs.kent.ac.uk:35357/v3/OS-FEDERATION/identity_providers/JaNet/protocols/abfab/auth\nIf this URL is not protected, the user can log in without any authentication.\nIf this URL is still valid in juno/kilo, I suggest that we point out to protect it with the entries:\n        Order allow,deny\n        Deny from all",
      "parentUuid": "9a80dd14_833dc42d",
      "revId": "e35272dc51e436d7445f1e1187b03abd451cfa46",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
